[0.000, "o", "x\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mWelcome to GNU Typist!\u001b[3;89H\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[4;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[4;89H\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[5;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mThis message is meant to get you started using gtypist. Please read the     \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[6;12H\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mmanual (at http://www.gnu.org/software/gtypist/doc/, or type \"info gtypist\")\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[7;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mfor more in-depth information!\u001b[7;89H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[8;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[8;89H\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[9;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mUse the arrow keys or PGUP/PGDN to scroll this window, SPACE/ENTER to start \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[10;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40musing gtypist, or 'D' to use gtypist and never show this dialog again.\u001b[89G\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[11;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[11;89H\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[12;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mThere are two types of typing exercises: \"drills\" and \"speed tests\". In a   \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[13;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\"drill\", gtypist displays text in every other line on the screen and waits  \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[14;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mfor the user to correctly type the exact same text in the intermediate\u001b[89G"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[15;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mlines. In a \"speed test\", gtypist displays text on the screen and waits     \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[16;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mfor the user to correctly type the exact same text over the top.\u001b[16;89H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[17;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[17;89H\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[18;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mIn both exercise types, you have to repeat the test if your error percentage\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[19;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mis higher than a maximum error percentage. The default is 3%, but if this is\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[20;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mtoo difficult you can change it by running gtypist with the \"-e <maxpct>\"   \u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[21;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mcommand-line option.\u001b[21;89H\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[22;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[22;89H\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[23;12H"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mOn most terminal emulators you can use Ctrl--/Ctrl-+ to resize the\u001b[23;89H\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[24;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mterminal window. For Mac OS X, Command--/Command-+ serve this purpose.\u001b[89G\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[25;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mOn Windows, change the properties of the terminal window by clicking on     \u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[26;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mthe top left corner of the window and choosing 'Properties'.\u001b[26;89H\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[27;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mx\u001b(B\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[27;89H\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m \u001b[28;12H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mmqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqqj\u001b(B\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\r\u001b[30d\u001b(0\u001b[0m\u001b[36m\u001b[40m\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mPress SPACE, ENTER or ESCAPE to start gtypist, or 'D' to disable this dialog\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[1.940, "o", "\r\u001b[2d\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[J\u001b[1;32H\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[36m\u001b[40mSeries selection menu\u001b[100G\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[3;19H\u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mThe following 10 lesson series are available\u001b[13;5H\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mSeries Q     Quick QWERTY course  (Q1 - Q5) \u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m    Series C     Colemak touch typing (C1 - C17)\u001b[14;5HSeries R     Long QWERTY course   (R1 - R14)    Series M     Typing drills\u001b[14;87H(M1 - M11)\u001b[15;5HSeries T     QWERTY touch typing  (T1 - T16)    Series S     Speed drills\u001b[15;87H(S1 - S4)\u001b[16;5HSeries V     Yet more QWERTY\u001b[39G"]
[0.000, "o", "(V1 - V19)    Series N     Calculator keypad    (N1 - N3)\u001b[17;5HSeries U     QWERTY Review\u001b[17;39H(U1 - U13)    More lessons...\u001b[18;5HSeries D     Dvorak touch typing  (D1 - D14)    Help...\r\u001b[30dUse arrowed keys to move around, SPACE or RETURN to select and ESCAPE to go back\u001b[18;97H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[1.797, "o", "\u001b[3;18H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;1m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mThe Q series contains the following 5 lessons\u001b[13;33H\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[1K "]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mLesson Q1     a s d f j k l ; e i\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[K\u001b[14;33H\u001b[1K Lesson Q2     h g o u n . t\u001b[K\u001b[15;33H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1K Lesson Q3     y r c , ? : p\u001b[K\u001b[16;33H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1K Lesson Q4     m w v z x b q\u001b[K\u001b[17;33H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1K "]
[0.000, "o", "Lesson Q5     ' -\u001b[K\r\u001b[18d\u001b[K\u001b[17;67H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[1.506, "o", "\u001b[2;25H\u001b[37m\u001b[40mWelcome to lesson Q1.\r\u001b[3d\u001b[K\u001b[4dIn the Q series of lessons, we will be learning to touch-type on the standard\r\u001b[5dkeyboard.  I will introduce you to each letter on the keyboard, one at a time.\r\u001b[6d"]
[0.000, "o", "By the time you have completed this series, you will be able to type the entire\r\u001b[7dalphabet, the numbers, and most of the punctuation keys by touch.\r\u001b[9d"]
[0.000, "o", "If you have never taken any lessons in typing before, please be patient.  Typing\r\u001b[10dis not difficult but it does take a lot of practice.  Avoid the tendency to\r\u001b[11d"]
[0.000, "o", "look down at your fingers while typing.  This is a very bad habit and is hard\r\u001b[12d"]
[0.000, "o", "to break later.  If you hit the wrong key, I will let you know.  (But, I won't\r\u001b[13d"]
[0.000, "o", "tell anyone else, so don't worry about it.)\u001b[K\r\u001b[14d\u001b[K\u001b[15d"]
[0.000, "o", "If you have always used the hunt-and-peck method, you will have an even harder\r\u001b[16d"]
[0.000, "o", "time keeping yourself from looking.  Don't be surprised if you find touch\r\u001b[17d"]
[0.000, "o", "typing slower than your old ways.  It may be slower when you first start.\r\u001b[18dBut, touch typing is far faster once you get the hang of it.\r\u001b[20dIf you can already touch type, you should be able to go through these lessons\r\u001b[21d"]
[0.000, "o", "fairly quickly.  Or, you may want to go directly to the S series.\r\u001b[30d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m Press RETURN or SPACE to continue, ESC to return to the menu \u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[18X\u001b[30;89H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m Tutorial \u001b[30;63H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[100G"]
[2.004, "o", "\r\u001b[2d\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[K\u001b[3;25HThe HOME Keys.\r\u001b[4d\u001b[K\u001b[5dIn order to hit the correct keys by touch alone, you must always know where your\r\u001b[6dfingers are.  The way to do this is to have a special place for each finger.\u001b[K\r\u001b[7dThis key is called the HOME position.\u001b[K\r\u001b[9d"]
[0.000, "o", "Place the first finger of your right hand on the J-key.  Now, place your second\u001b[K\r\u001b[10d"]
[0.001, "o", "finger on the K-key, your third finger on the L-key, and your fourth-finger on\r\u001b[11dthe ;-key (the one with the : and ; on it).\u001b[K\r\u001b[12d\u001b[K\u001b[13d"]
[0.000, "o", "Similarly place the four fingers of your left hand on the F, D, S, and A-keys.\r\u001b[14d"]
[0.000, "o", "Place your right thumb over the SPACE bar.  (Henceforth, always hit the SPACE\r\u001b[15dbar with this thumb.)  Now, lift all your fingers slightly so that they are\u001b[K\r\u001b[16d"]
[0.000, "o", "poised just over the keys.  Each finger should be just barely touching its home\r\u001b[17d"]
[0.000, "o", "key.  This is an electronic keyboard and does not take much pressure to ac-\r\u001b[18d"]
[0.000, "o", "cidentally press the key down"]
[0.000, "o", ".\u001b[K\r\u001b[20dAbove the D-key is the E-key.  Above the K-key is the I-key.  Learn these\u001b[K\r\u001b[21d"]
[0.000, "o", "positions well.  Whenever you are about to type a line, look at your fingers and\r\u001b[22dmake sure they are in the HOME position.  Then don't look at them again.\u001b[30;63H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[100G"]
[1.606, "o", "\u001b[3;25H\u001b[37m\u001b[40mDRILL PATTERNS\r\u001b[5dFor the rest of this lesson, I will display a line of text in the middle of the\u001b[K\r\u001b[6dscreen and instructions at the top of the screen.\u001b[K\r\u001b[7d\u001b[K\u001b[8dAll you have to do is type in the characters that you see in the middle of\r\u001b[9dthe screen.  If you hit the correct key, I will not do anything.  If you make\u001b[K\r\u001b[10d"]
[0.000, "o", "a mistake, I will display a large X under the letter that you got wrong and\u001b[K\r\u001b[11dbeep the terminal. In either event, just k"]
[0.000, "o", "eep going by typing the next letter.\r\u001b[13d"]
[0.000, "o", "When you have finished typing the line, hit the RETURN key.  To do this, extend\r\u001b[14d"]
[0.000, "o", "the little finger of your right hand over to the RETURN key.  Hit the key and\r\u001b[15d"]
[0.000, "o", "zip the finger back to its home position.  Be careful not to let your other\r\u001b[16dfingers move far from their home positions in the process.  Also, be careful\u001b[K\r\u001b[17dnot to type an extra space at the end of the line.\u001b[K\r\u001b[18d\u001b[K\u001b[19d"]
[0.000, "o", "If you made no mistakes on the line, I will display the next drill pattern.  If\r\u001b[20dyou did make a mistake, I will beep at you and make you do the line again.  If\r\u001b[21d"]
[0.000, "o", "on the second try you made more than two mistakes, I will beep again and make\u001b[K\r\u001b[22dyou try again, etc.  Don't forget to use your right thumb for the SPACE bar.\u001b[30;63H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[100G"]
[1.606, "o", "\r\u001b[2d\u001b[37m\u001b[40m(1) Try this:\r\u001b[3d\u001b[K\u001b[4dasdf ;lkj asdf ;lkj asdf ;lkj asdf ;lkj asdf ;lkj asdf ;lkj\r\u001b[5d\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m \u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[K\u001b[6d\b\u001b[K\u001b[8d\u001b[K\u001b[9d\u001b[K\u001b[10d\u001b[K\u001b[11d\u001b[K\u001b[13d\u001b[K\u001b[14d\u001b[K\u001b[15d\u001b[K\u001b[16d\u001b[K\u001b[17d\u001b[K\u001b[19d\u001b[K\u001b[20d\u001b[K\u001b[21d\u001b[K\u001b[22d\u001b[K\u001b[30;88H\u001b[1K \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m  Drill  \r\u001b[5d \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[30;100H"]
[0.500, "o", "\r\u001b[5d\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[K\u001b[30;100H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[0.501, "o", "\r\u001b[5d\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m \u001b[30;100H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
[0.500, "o", "\r\u001b[5d\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[K\u001b[30;100H\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
